| Status Code | Meaning                |
| ----------- | ---------------------- |
| 200         | OK                     |
| 301         | Permanently Redirected |
| 302         | Temporarily Redirected |
| 400         | Bad Request            |
| 401         | Unauthorized           |
| 403         | Forbidden              |
| 404         | Not Found              |
| 500         | Internal Server Error  |

## 🧩 HTTP Headers

Headers provide additional information about an HTTP request or response.

Examples include:

```text
Content-Type
User-Agent
Host
Cookie
Authorization
```

## 🍪 Cookies

Cookies are small pieces of data stored by a browser.

Websites can use cookies for things such as:

* Sessions
* Preferences
* Authentication
* Tracking

## 🔒 HTTP vs HTTPS

HTTP sends web traffic without the encryption provided by TLS.

HTTPS uses TLS to protect communication between the browser and server.

This helps provide:

* Confidentiality
* Integrity
* Server authentication

